hadiths[216]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8275","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that Allah عزوجل, when He created disease, created its medicine, so seek treatment. > **""Verily Allah عزوجل, when He created disease, created the cure, so seek treatment.""**"
"8276","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said Allah عزوجل sent down no disease but sent down its cure, known to whoever knows it and unknown to whoever remains ignorant of it. > **""Allah عزوجل sent down no disease but sent down for it a cure; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it.""**"
"8277","A man of the Ansar reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a wounded man and ordered that the physician of Banu Fulan be called for him. When asked whether medicine avails anything, he declared glorification of Allah and affirmed no disease descends in the earth but Allah has made healing for it. > **""Call for him the physician of Banu Fulan. Glory be to Allah! Allah تبارك وتعالى sent down no disease in the earth but made for it healing.""**"
"8278","Abu Said al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reports from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Allah sent down no disease but sent down its medicine, known or unknown, except al-Sam. When asked what al-Sam is, he said death. > **""Allah sent down no disease but sent down for it medicine, known to whoever knows it and unknown to whoever is ignorant of it, except al-Sam.""** > **""Death.""**"
"8279","Abu Musa رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that Allah تبارك وتعالى sent down no disease but sent down healing for it, and enjoined cow milk, for it grazes from every tree. > **""Allah تبارك وتعالى sent down no disease but sent down for it healing, so hold to cow milk, for it grazes from all the trees.""**"
"8280","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people commanding treatment, for Allah عزوجل created no disease but created healing for it except al-Sam, which is death. > **""O people, seek treatment, for Allah عزوجل created no disease but created for it healing except al-Sam, and al-Sam is death.""**"
"8281","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether medicine benefits against decree. He replied that medicine is itself from decree and may benefit by Allah's permission. > **""Medicine is from the decree, and it may benefit by Allah's permission.""**"
"8282","Hakim ibn Hizam رضي الله عنه reports asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether incantations used for healing and medicines used for treatment repel anything of Allah's decree. He replied they are Allah's decree. > **""They are Allah's تعالى decree.""**"
"8283","Al-Harith ibn Sa'd reports from his father that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether ruqyah and medicines repel divine decree. He replied they are Allah's decree. > **""They are Allah's decree.""**"
"8284","Safwan ibn Assal رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ described Allah's عزوجل western gate for repentance spanning seventy years, unclosed until the sun rises from the west, and angels spreading wings for the seeker of knowledge in approval. The Bedouins asked for the best gift to a servant, and he named good character. Then asked whether to seek treatment, he affirmed the Sender of disease sent medicine for every disease except one, which is old age. > **""Verily Allah عزوجل has opened a gate from the west whose extent is seventy years, for repentance; He will not close it until the sun rises from its west. No man goes out seeking knowledge but the angels spread their wings for him in pleasure with what he does.""** > **""Good character. Do you not know that He Who sent down disease sent down medicine, and sent down no disease but sent down for it medicine, except one disease? Old age.""**"
"8285","Wahb ibn Jusham reports that he gave Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه a medicine for loosening the bowels."
"8286","Al-Amash reports hearing Hayyan, grandfather of Ibn Abjar the elder, say to leave medicine while the body can endure the illness."
"8287","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that her daughter complained, so she prepared nabidh for her in a brass vessel. The Prophet ﷺ entered while it fermented and asked what it was. When told, he declared Allah عزوجل did not place healing in the unlawful. > **""What is this? Verily Allah عزوجل did not place your healing in the unlawful.""**"
"8288","Umm al-Darda رضي الله عنها reports from the Prophet ﷺ that Allah created disease and medicine, so seek treatment but do not treat with the unlawful. > **""Verily Allah created disease and medicine, so seek treatment, and do not treat with the unlawful.""**"
"8289","Abu Wail reports that a man among them fell ill and an intoxicant was prescribed for him. They came to Abdullah رضي الله عنه and asked him, and he said Allah did not place healing in what He prohibited for them."
"8290","Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade forcing the sick to eat, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink. > **""Do not force your sick to eat, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink.""**"
"8291","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ likened the stomach to the basin of the body with veins leading to it; if sound, health flows to the veins, and if corrupt, sickness flows. > **""The stomach is the basin of the body, and the veins lead to it; if the stomach is sound the veins issue with health, and if the stomach is corrupt the veins issue with sickness.""**"
"8292","Abu Said al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that drinking water upon an empty stomach diminishes strength. > **""Whoever drinks water upon an empty stomach, his strength is diminished.""**"
"8293","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that much laughter degrades one's due, and drinking water on an empty stomach diminishes strength. > **""Whoever laughs much, his right is belittled, and whoever drinks water on an empty stomach, his strength is diminished.""**"
"8294","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the flank is the kidney vein which harms its owner when stirred, so treat it with heated water and honey. > **""The flank is the kidney vein; when it moves it harms its owner, so treat it with heated water and honey.""**"
"8295","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that when the Prophet ﷺ complained, he would take a handful of black seed and drink water and honey over it."
"8296","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reports being with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among forty-two companions while the Prophet ﷺ prayed toward the Maqam. After prayer he reached between himself and the Kabah as if taking something, then explained Paradise was shown to him and a cluster of grapes pleased him but eluded him; had he taken it he would have planted it for them to eat Paradise fruit. He then taught that truffle is medicine for the eye, Ajwa is from Paradise fruit, and this black seed found in salt is medicine for every disease except death. > **""Did you see me when I finished my prayer reaching between me and the Kabah as if to take something? Paradise was shown to me and I never saw its like. A cluster of grapes passed me and pleased me, so I reached to take it but it eluded me. Had I taken it I would have planted it among you so you would eat from Paradise fruit. Know that truffle is medicine for the eye, Ajwa is from Paradise fruit, and this black seed in salt is medicine for every disease except death.""**"
"8297","Usamah ibn Sharik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said black seed is healing for every disease except al-Sam. > **""Black seed is healing for every disease except al-Sam.""**"
"8298","Amr ibn Hurayth reports from his father, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that truffle is from al-Salwa, and its water is healing for the eye. > **""Truffle is from al-Salwa, and its water is healing for the eye.""**"
"8299","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said camel milk and urine contain healing for those whose stomachs are loose. > **""In camel milk and urine is healing for those whose stomachs are loose.""**"
"8300","Sa'd ibn Abi Rafi reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited him in illness, placed his hand between his breasts until its coolness reached his heart, and said he was afflicted in the heart. He directed him to al-Harith ibn Kaladah, a practitioner of medicine, to take five Ajwa dates of Medina, crush them with their stones, and rub him with them. > **""You are a man afflicted in the heart, so go to al-Harith ibn Kaladah, for he practices medicine. Let him take five dates of Medina Ajwa, crush them with their stones, and rub you with them.""**"
"8301","A man of the Ansar reports from his father that the Prophet ﷺ prescribed for sciatica the fat tail of an Arab ram, neither small nor large, melted then divided into three parts, drinking one part each day on an empty stomach. > **""Take the fat tail of an Arab ram, neither small nor large, melt it, divide it into three parts, and drink one part each day on an empty stomach.""**"
"8302","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ used to prescribe for sciatica the tail of an Arab ram neither large nor small, divided into three parts, melted, drinking one part each day. > **""The tail of an Arab ram neither large nor small, divided into three parts, melted, drinking one part each day.""**"
"8303","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ that whoever buys or is gifted a ram should divide it, meaning the fat tail, into three parts, feeding one part each day on an empty stomach, whether melted or eaten as food, as treatment for sciatica. > **""Whoever buys a ram, or is gifted one, let him divide it into three parts and feed one part each day on an empty stomach; if he wishes he melts it, and if he wishes he eats it as food, as treatment for sciatica.""**"
"8304","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said truffle is from manna and its water healing for the eye, Ajwa is from Paradise and healing from poison. He also prescribed for sciatica the ram tail divided into three, melted, drinking one part daily on an empty stomach. > **""Truffle is from manna, and its water is healing for the eye; Ajwa is from Paradise, and it is healing from poison.""**"
"8305","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said eating seven Medina Ajwa dates by day protects from poison that day, and eating them by night protects from poison. > **""Whoever eats seven dates of Medina Ajwa in a day, poison will not harm him that day; and whoever eats them at night, poison will not harm him.""**"
"8306","Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded honoring the palm, one's paternal aunt, created from the clay of Adam, the only tree grafted. He also commanded feeding women in childbirth fresh ripe dates, or dry dates if none, and named the tree under which Maryam bint Imran stayed as most noble to Allah. > **""Honor your aunt the palm, for it was created from the clay from which Adam was created, and there is no tree grafted besides it.""** > **""Feed your women in childbirth fresh dates; if there are no fresh dates, then dry dates. There is no tree more noble to Allah than the tree under which Maryam bint Imran stayed.""**"
"8307","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Salamah, or Aishah, finding a boy whose nostrils flowed with blood due to udhra. He rebuked tormenting children and said a woman need only take Indian costus, rub it with seven dates, then administer it to him. Ibn Abi Utbah added, then drip it into his nose. They did so and he healed. > **""Why do you torment your children? It suffices one of you to take Indian costus, rub it with seven dates, then administer it to him.""**"
"8308","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a boy whose nostrils flowed with blood. He asked why they frighten children and ordered marine costus administered as nasal drops, for in it is healing from seven remedies, one being pleurisy. > **""Why do you torment your children? Take marine costus and administer it to him as nasal drops, for in it is healing from seven remedies, one being pleurisy.""**"
"8309","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her and asked why she appeared weakened. She said she drank a laxative medicine, namely shubrum. He asked what she had to do with shubrum, for it is hot and harsh, and enjoined senna and sannut, for in them is medicine for everything except al-Sam. The rest is in adornment. > **""What have you to do with shubrum? It is hot and harsh. Upon you is senna and sannut, for in them is medicine for everything except al-Sam.""**"
"8310","Asma bint Abi Bakr رضي الله عنها reports seeing the Prophet ﷺ in a dream after his death asking whether the Quran is altered. She answered affirmatively in meaning. Asked about her sons, she said they suffer severe constipation. He looked to one of his wives, as if Hafsah bint Umar, and ordered a remedy for her sons, declaring he does not heal from al-Sam. The wife gave black seed like shuniz or leek seed, red earth, and a string of pearls. Thereafter when any child of Asma among the tribes complained, a cup was filled with water, red earth, leek seed, shuniz, and pearl string added, then poured over him."
"8311","Zuhayr reports from a woman of his family, from Mulaykah bint Amr of the descendants of Zayd ibn Sad, that she complained of throat pain and was given cow ghee, citing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that its milk is healing, its clarified butter medicine, and its meat disease. > **""Its milk is healing, its clarified butter is medicine, and its meat is disease.""**"
"8312","Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said if healing lies in anything, it is in a cupping incision, a drink of honey, or cautery striking pain, though he dislikes cautery and does not love it. > **""If there is healing in anything, it is in a cupping incision, a drink of honey, or cautery striking pain; and I dislike cautery, I do not love it.""**"
"8313","Muawiyah ibn Hadij رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said if healing lies in anything, it is in a cupping incision, a drink of honey, or cautery with fire striking pain, though he does not love to be cauterized. > **""If there is healing in anything, it is in a cupping incision, a drink of honey, or cautery with fire striking pain; and I do not love to be cauterized.""**"
"8314","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ said if any of their medicines contains healing, it is in a cupping incision, or, as the narrator thinks, a lick of honey. > **""If there is healing in any of your medicines, it is in a cupping incision, or a lick of honey.""**"
"8315","Al-Saib ibn Yazid رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded cupping and said people never sought a better bleeding remedy than it, or a drink of honey. > **""No bleeding remedy has come over people better than it, or a drink of honey.""**"
"8316","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ that on the night of ascension he passed no heaven but the angels said to order his nation to cup, and to use costus and black seed. > **""I passed no heaven among the heavens but the angels said: O Muhammad, order your nation to cup, and to use costus and black seed.""**"
"8317","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined cupping and marine costus. > **""Upon you is cupping and marine costus.""**"
"8318","Malik ibn Sasah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the night he was taken, he passed no assembly of angels but they ordered him to cup. > **""I passed no assembly of angels on the night I was taken but they ordered me to cup.""**"
"8319","Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali reports entering upon Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه while he cupped and was asked whether he would cup, having never cupped. Abu Hurayrah conveyed that Abu al-Qasim ﷺ told that Gabriel informed him cupping is the most beneficial treatment of people. > **""Gabriel informed him that cupping is the most beneficial treatment of people.""**"
"8320","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that Abu Taybah cupped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Uyaynah ibn Hisn, or al-Aqra ibn Habis, entered and asked what it was, and he replied it is cupping, the best treatment. > **""This is cupping, and it is the best of what you treat with.""**"
"8321","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ was cupped in the two jugular veins and between the shoulders."
"8322","Abu Umayyah al-Fazari رضي الله عنه reports seeing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cupping."
"8323","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi reports from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said five are from the ways of the messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, siwak, and perfume. > **""Five are from the ways of the messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, siwak, and perfume.""**"
"8324","Samurah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ summoned a cupper who cupped him with a horn and incised with a blade. A man of Banu Fazarah asked why he lets him cut his flesh, and he asked whether he knew what cupping is, the best treatment. > **""Do you know what this is? This is cupping, and it is the best of what you treat with.""**"
"8325","Abdullah ibn Jafar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ was cupped after being poisoned."
"8326","Ali رضي الله عنه reports, as far as he knows from the Prophet ﷺ, that when blood boils in one of them, let him shed it even with an arrowhead. > **""When blood boils in one of you, let him shed it even with an arrowhead.""**"
"8327","Al-Husayn ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said there is an hour on Friday in which none is cupped but dies. > **""In Friday there is an hour in which none is cupped but dies.""**"
"8328","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that whoever is cupped on Wednesday or Saturday then suffers whiteness should blame only himself. > **""Whoever is cupped on Wednesday or Saturday then suffers whiteness, let him blame none but himself.""**"
"8329","He repeated it with his chain except saying whoever is cupped on Wednesday and Saturday. > **""Whoever is cupped on Wednesday and Saturday.""**"
"8330","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما enjoins cupping on the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first, lest blood rage and kill."
"8331","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said Surah al-Hadid descended on Tuesday, Allah created iron on Tuesday, the son of Adam killed his brother on Tuesday, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cupping on Tuesday. > **""Surah al-Hadid descended on Tuesday, Allah created iron on Tuesday, the son of Adam killed his brother on Tuesday.""**"
"8332","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports entering upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he cupped on Tuesday, the seventeenth of the month. When asked, he affirmed and said whoever among them finds Tuesday the seventeenth should not pass it until cupped. > **""Yes. Whoever among you finds Tuesday the seventeenth of the month, let him not pass it until he is cupped, so be cupped.""**"
"8333","Maqil ibn Yasar رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said cupping on Tuesday the seventeenth of the month is medicine for the year's disease. > **""Cupping on Tuesday the seventeenth of the month is medicine for the year's disease.""**"
"8334","Muhammad ibn Sirin said the most beneficial cupping is in the waning of the month."
"8335","Abu Said al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said cupping in the middle of the head is medicine for madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and molars, and he named it Umm Munqidh. > **""Cupping in the middle of the head is medicine for madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and molars.""**"
"8336","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said cupping in the head is medicine for madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and molars. > **""Cupping in the head is medicine for madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and molars.""**"
"8337","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ used to cup in the front of his head and named it Umm Mughith."
"8338","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said head cupping heals its owner from seven ills: madness, headache, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, molar pain, and darkness found in the eyes. > **""Cupping in the head is healing for its owner from seven ills: madness, headache, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, molar pain, and darkness he finds in his eyes.""**"
"8339","Suhayb رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined cupping in the hollow of the skull, for it is medicine for seventy-two ills including madness, leprosy, vitiligo, and molar pain, as found in the heard original. > **""Upon you is cupping in the hollow of the skull, for it is medicine for seventy-two ills, and five ills of madness, leprosy, vitiligo, and molar pain.""**"
"8340","Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn al-Walid used to cup his crown and between his shoulders. Asked about it, he cited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cupping his crown and saying whoever sheds this blood is unharmed if he takes no other medicine. > **""Whoever sheds this blood, it will not harm him not to treat with anything.""**"
"8341","Umm Sad, wife of Zayd ibn Thabit رضي الله عنها, reports hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ order burial of blood when cupped."
"8342","Abu Bashir al-Ansari رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ concerning fever to cool it with water, for it is from the heat of Hell. > **""Cool it with water, for it is from the heat of Hell.""**"
"8343","Samurah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said fever is a piece of Fire, so cool it with cold water. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ suffered fever he would call for a water skin, empty it upon his head, and bathe. > **""Fever is a piece of Fire, so cool it from you with cold water.""**"
"8344","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when one of them suffers fever, let cold morning water be poured over him for three nights. > **""When one of you suffers fever, let cold morning water be poured over him for three nights.""**"
"8345","Rafi ibn Khadij رضي الله عنه reports that Nuayman said he suffered severe feverish pain. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked where he was regarding Mahayah, which was an unhealthy land. > **""Where are you, O Nuayman, regarding Mahayah?""**"
"8346","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Muraffa reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided Khaybar with eighteen hundred, conquered it green with fruits, and the people fell to them and were seized by fever. They complained, and he said fever is the harbinger of death and Allah's prison on earth, so cool water in skins and pour it between the two calls of Maghrib and Isha. They did so and it left. They reported back, and he said no vessel filled is worse than a belly; if they must, make a third for food, a third for drink, and a third for breath. He divided it into eighteen shares. > **""Fever is the harbinger of death, and it is Allah's prison on earth, so cool water for it in skins and pour it upon you between the two calls: the call of Maghrib and the call of Isha.""** > **""No vessel when filled is worse than a belly; if you must do, make it a third for food, a third for drink, and a third for wind or breath.""**"
"8347","Abdullah ibn al-Muraffa reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar with eighteen hundred, divided into eighteen shares, a share per hundred. It was green with fruits; they ate and fever kneaded them. They complained, and he said this fever is the harbinger of death, Allah's prison on earth, a piece of Fire; when it seizes them cool water in skins and pour between the two prayers, meaning Maghrib and Isha. > **""O people, this fever is the harbinger of death, Allah's prison on earth, a piece of Fire; when it seizes you, cool water for it in skins, meaning water skins, and pour upon you between the two prayers.""**"
"8348","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that when revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ he suffered headache, so he would wrap his head with henna."
"8349","Salma, wife of Abu Rafi رضي الله عنها, reports serving the Prophet ﷺ, and no ulcer or injury befell him but he ordered her to place henna upon it."
"8350","One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ reports that the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and asked whether she had dharurah. She said yes, so he called for it, placed it upon a pustule between his toes, then prayed to Allah the Diminisher of the great and Augmenter of the small to extinguish it, and it was extinguished. > **""Have you dharurah? O Allah, Diminisher of the great and Augmenter of the small, extinguish it from me.""**"
"8351","Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه says to eat pomegranate with its pulp, for it tans the stomach."
"8352","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the best of their kohl is ithmid, which grows hair and clears vision. > **""The best of your kohl is ithmid; it grows hair and clears vision.""**"
"8353","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined ithmid, for it grows hair, removes filth, and clarifies vision. > **""Upon you is ithmid, for it grows hair, removes filth, and clarifies vision.""**"
"8354","Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when one applies kohl let him apply in odd number, and when he cleans with stones let him use odd number. > **""When one of you applies kohl, let him apply in odd number; and when he cleans with stones, let him clean in odd number.""**"
"8355","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to apply kohl in odd number."
"8356","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ applied kohl, he placed three in the right eye and two strokes in the left eye, making it odd."
"8357","Samurah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said Satan has a kohl and a licking; when man kohl from his kohl it distracts him from prayer, and when he licks from his licking his tongue hastens to evil. > **""Satan has a kohl and a licking; when man kohls from his kohl it distracts him from prayer, and when he licks from his licking his tongue hastens to evil.""**"
"8358","Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه reports entering upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while a black boy massaged his back. Asked, he said the she-camel threw him. > **""The she-camel threw me.""**"
"8359","Salman رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever feeds a sick person his craving, Allah feeds him from Paradise fruit. > **""Whoever feeds a sick person his craving, Allah feeds him from the fruits of Paradise.""**"
"8360","Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda reports from his mother, from her grandmother, that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether rage harms. He said yes, as beating harms trees. > **""Yes, as beating harms trees.""**"
"8361","Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cautery, disliked drinking hot water, and when he applied kohl applied in odd, and when he cleaned with stones used odd."
"8362","Sa'd al-Tafri رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade cautery and said he dislikes drinking hot water. > **""I dislike drinking hot water.""**"
"8363","Salamah ibn al-Akwa رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said fire heals no one. > **""Fire heals no one.""**"
"8364","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه reports that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ with his brother whose belly was swollen with dropsy. He asked whether to cauterize as physicians ordered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not to cauterize and returned him to his family. A camel passed and struck the belly, so it subsided. Brought to the Prophet ﷺ, he said had they gone to physicians they would claim fire healed him. > **""Do not cauterize him, and return him to his family. Had you brought him to physicians you would say: fire healed him.""**"
"8365","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the place of cautery is warm poultice, the place of throat remedy is nasal drops, and the place of blowing is side-mouth medicine. > **""The place of cautery is poultice, the place of throat remedy is nasal drops, and the place of blowing is side-mouth medicine.""**"
"8366","Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf reports from Abu Umamah Sad ibn Zurarah, a chief on Aqabah, that a thorn seized him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited him and said twice what an evil death for the Jews who say why did he not defend his companion, though he owns him neither harm nor benefit, yet he will strive for him. He was cauterized with two lines above his head and died. > **""What an evil death for the Jews who say: why did he not defend his companion? I own him neither harm nor benefit, yet I shall strive for him.""**"
"8367","One of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized Sad, or Sad ibn Zurarah, in his throat for dhubhah, and said he leaves no unease in himself concerning Sad, or Asad ibn Zurarah. > **""I leave no unease in myself concerning Sad.""**"
"8368","Ubayy ibn Kab رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ cauterized him."
"8369","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Asad ibn Zurarah reports from his uncle that Abu Umamah suffered a pain Medina folk call dhabh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said he would excuse himself concerning Abu Umamah. He cauterized him by hand and he died, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it is an evil death for the Jews who say why did he not defend his companion, though he owns him and himself nothing against Allah. > **""I shall surely excuse myself concerning Abu Umamah. An evil death for the Jews who say: why did he not defend his companion? I own for him and myself nothing against Allah.""**"
"8370","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Prophet ﷺ ordered that Ibn Zurarah be cauterized."
"8371","Sahl ibn Hunayf رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Asad ibn Zurarah to visit him for pain from a thorn, cauterized him on his shoulder, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it is the worst death for the Jews who say his companion treated him but it did not benefit him. > **""The worst death for the Jews who say: his companion treated him but it did not benefit him.""**"
"8372","Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Asad ibn Zurarah with a pain called shawkah, cauterized him on his neck, and he died. The Prophet ﷺ said what an evil dead for the Jews who say his companion treated him but it did not benefit him. > **""What an evil dead for the Jews who say: his companion treated him but it did not benefit him.""**"
"8373","Kab ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited al-Bara ibn Marur seized by dhubhah, and ordered one to incise him with fire to direct him aright."
"8374","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, reports that people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying a companion complained, shall they cauterize him. He was silent a while then said if they wish cauterize, and if they wish heat stones for him. > **""If you wish, cauterize him; and if you wish, heat stones for him.""**"
"8375","Ata ibn al-Saib reports coming to Abu Abd al-Rahman while he cauterized a boy. Asked, he said yes, it is the Arab medicine. Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه cited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Allah عزوجل sent down no disease but sent down with it medicine, unknown or known. > **""Verily Allah عزوجل sent down no disease but sent down with it medicine; whoever is ignorant is ignorant, and whoever knows knows.""**"
"8376","Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه reports entering with the Prophet ﷺ upon an Ansari man with a swelling. The Prophet ﷺ asked why they do not remove it from him. It was lanced while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ witnessed. > **""Will you not remove it from him?""**"
"8377","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that two brother men came to Medina while a companion of the Prophet ﷺ was struck by an arrow in his body. The Prophet ﷺ told his kin to seek one to treat him. The two brothers were brought, and asked whether they treat with iron. They said they treated in Jahiliyyah. The Prophet ﷺ said treat him, so he lanced him until he healed. > **""With iron do you treat? Treat him.""**"
"8378","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that a wounded man came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking permission to lance it, and he permitted him."
"8379","Abdullah ibn Yahya al-Hadrami reports that Hayyan ibn Abjar al-Kinani opened the belly of a woman he married until he treated her."
"8380","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said growth of hair in the nose is safety from leprosy. > **""Growth of hair in the nose is safety from leprosy.""**"
"8381","Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ to hold to this blessed tree, olive oil, and treat with it, for it heals piles. > **""Upon you is this blessed tree, olive oil, so treat with it, for it heals piles.""**"
"8382","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Prophet ﷺ said to clean with cold water, for it heals piles. > **""Clean with cold water, for it heals piles.""**"
"8383","Al-Mustawrid al-Fihri رضي الله عنه reports that a man with gout came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said midday heats belied him. > **""Midday heats have belied you.""**"
"8384","Tariq ibn Shihab reports that a man saw another with khanazir and said were it not a pledge he would narrate. It reached Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, who met him and told him to narrate, expiate the oath, for the pledge was improper. He said to take urine of arak-eating camels, cook it until thick then drink it, and take arak leaves, pound and sprinkle upon it. He did so and healed."
"8385","Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ not to gaze constantly at lepers, and when speaking to them keep a spear's length between. > **""Do not gaze constantly at lepers, and when you speak to them let there be a spear's length between you and them.""**"
"8386","Al-Husayn ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ the same: not to gaze constantly at lepers, and keep a spear's length when speaking. > **""Do not gaze constantly at lepers, and when you speak to them let there be a spear's length between you and them.""**"
"8387","Muadh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not to gaze constantly at lepers. > **""Do not gaze constantly at lepers.""**"
"8388","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ not to gaze constantly at lepers. > **""Do not gaze constantly at lepers.""**"
"8389","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports from the Prophet ﷺ that growth of hair in the nose is safety from leprosy. > **""Growth of hair in the nose is safety from leprosy.""**"
"8390","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said no contagion, no omen, no envy, and the evil eye is real. > **""No contagion, no omen, no envy, and the evil eye is real.""**"
"8391","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said no Safar, no Hamah, and no sick transmits to a sound one. > **""No Safar, no Hamah, and no sick transmits to a sound one.""**"
"8392","Abu Talhah al-Khawlani reports that Umayr ibn Sad sat among Palestinians, called unique, upon a great bench, ordering his boy to water horses from a stone basin, including a mangy mare dripping blood or water. One said all horses would mange. He ordered it watered, citing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that no contagion, no omen, no Hamah; consider the camel in the desert sound in its chest then afflicted without prior cause, who infected the first. > **""No contagion, no omen, no Hamah. Have you not seen the camel in the desert, sound in its chest or flanks, then afflicted without prior cause? Who infected the first?""**"
"8393","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said no contagion, no Hamah, so who infected the first. > **""No contagion, no Hamah, so who infected the first?""**"
"8394","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said no contagion. A Bedouin said they take a mangy sheep, cast it among sheep, and they mange. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked who mangied the first. > **""No contagion. O Bedouin, who mangied the first?""**"
"8395","Abu Talhah al-Khawlani reports entering upon Umayr ibn Sad among Palestinians, mentioning contagion, and he cited hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say no contagion, no omen, no Ham, with a long story. > **""No contagion, no omen, no Ham.""**"
"8396","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said no contagion, no Safar, no Ham, and two months are never thirty days together. Fuller in blood-money concerning one killing a dhimmi. > **""No contagion, no Safar, no Ham, and two months are never thirty days.""**"
"8397","Al-Hasan reports Anas رضي الله عنه was asked about nushrah and said it was mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked and said it is Satan's work. > **""It is from Satan's work.""**"
"8398","Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه reports hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say whoever attaches a tamimah, Allah fulfills not for him, and whoever hangs a wadaah, Allah grants him no ease. > **""Whoever attaches a tamimah, Allah fulfills not for him; and whoever hangs a wadaah, Allah grants him no ease.""**"
"8399","Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani رضي الله عنه reports that a group came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he pledged nine and withheld one. Asked why, he said upon him is a tamimah. The man inserted his hand and cut it, so he pledged him and said whoever hangs a tamimah commits shirk. > **""Upon him is a tamimah. Whoever hangs a tamimah commits shirk.""**"
"8400","Isa reports entering upon Abu Mabad to visit him and asking why he hangs nothing. He said death is nearer, citing hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say whoever hangs something is entrusted to it. > **""Whoever hangs something is entrusted to it.""**"
"8401","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said he cares not what he commits if he drinks tiryaq, hangs a tamimah, or utters poetry from himself. > **""I care not what I commit, or what I incur, if I drink tiryaq, hang a tamimah, or utter poetry from myself.""**"
"8402","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a ring, apparently of brass, upon a man's upper arm and asked woe what it was. He said for wahinah. He said it increases only weakness; cast it off, for if he dies with it he never prospers. In another wording, he is entrusted to it. In a stopped wording, cast it, for dying believing it benefits is dying upon other than fitrah. > **""Woe to you, what is this? It increases you only weakness. Cast it from you, for if you die with it upon you, you will never prosper.""**"
"8403","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه reports seeing a brass ring upon a man's arm for wahinah and warning dying with it entrusts him to it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not of us is who takes omens or has them taken, practices soothsaying or has it done, or, as he thinks, practices magic or has it done. > **""He who dies with it upon him is entrusted to it. Not of us is who takes omens or has omens taken for him, practices soothsaying or has it practiced for him, or practices magic or has it practiced for him.""**"
"8404","Abu Hassan reports that a man of Banu Amir entered upon Aishah رضي الله عنها telling that Abu Hurayrah narrates from the Prophet ﷺ that omen lies in house, woman, and horse. She angered greatly and swore by Who revealed the Quran upon Muhammad ﷺ he never said it; rather he said Jahiliyyah folk took omens from that. > **""The people of Jahiliyyah used to take omens from that.""**"
"8405","In a narration Aishah رضي الله عنها says the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to say Jahiliyyah folk said omen lies in house, woman, and horse. Then Aishah recited the verse that no calamity befalls earth or selves but in a Book. > **""The people of Jahiliyyah used to say: omen lies in house, woman, and horse.""**"
"8406","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said evil omen lies in house, woman, and horse, with a variant if omen lies in anything. > **""Evil lies in house, woman, and horse.""**"
"8407","Umar رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said evil lies in three: mount, dwelling, and woman. > **""Evil lies in three: mount, dwelling, and woman.""**"
"8408","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports mentioning omen before the Messenger ﷺ, with mention of woman, house, mount. The Prophet ﷺ said if any lies in anything, it lies in good omen. > **""If any of it lies in anything, it lies in good omen.""**"
"8409","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that folk came to the Prophet ﷺ saying they entered this house prosperous, numerous, harmonious, then became poor, few, discordant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said leave it while blameworthy. Asked how, he said sell it or gift it. > **""Leave it while blameworthy. Sell it or gift it.""**"
"8410","Sahl ibn Harithah al-Ansari رضي الله عنه reports that folk complained to the Prophet ﷺ they dwelt in a house numerous then diminished. He asked why they did not leave it while blameworthy. > **""Why did you not leave it while blameworthy?""**"
"8411","Asma bint Umays رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said among man's worldly wretchedness are three: bad house, bad woman, bad mount. Asked, he defined bad house as narrow courtyard and evil neighbors; bad mount as refusing its back and evil temper; bad woman as barren womb and evil temper. > **""Among man's worldly wretchedness are three: bad house, bad woman, bad mount. Bad house is narrow courtyard and evil neighbors; bad mount refuses its back and evil temper; bad woman is barren womb and evil temper.""**"
"8412","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever is turned by omen from a need commits shirk. Asked its expiation, he said to say O Allah no good but Your good, no omen but Your omen, no god but You. > **""Whoever is turned by omen from a need commits shirk. Let one say: O Allah, no good but Your good, no omen but Your omen, no god but You.""**"
"8413","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reports omen mentioned before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said whoever is struck yet must proceed, dearer to us than such, let him say O Allah no omen but Yours, no good but Yours, no god but You. > **""Whoever is struck by that yet must proceed, let him say: O Allah, no omen but Your omen, no good but Your good, no god but You.""**"
"8414","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said thrice no bird but Your bird. > **""No bird but Your bird.""**"
"8415","Ruwayfi ibn Thabit رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever is turned by omen from something approaches shirk. > **""Whoever is turned by omen from something approaches shirk.""**"
"8416","Habis al-Tamimi رضي الله عنه reports hearing the Prophet ﷺ say nothing in Ham, the evil eye is real, and truest divination is good omen. > **""Nothing in Ham, the evil eye is real, and truest divination is good omen.""**"
"8417","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said nothing in Ham, the evil eye is real, and truest divination is good omen. > **""Nothing in Ham, the evil eye is real, and truest divination is good omen.""**"
"8418","Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked who conveys their milch camels. A man stood saying I. Asked his name, he said Sakhr or Jandal. He bade him sit. Asked again, another stood named Yaish, and he bade him convey. > **""Who conveys our milch camels? What is your name? Sit. Who conveys our milch camel milk? What is your name? Convey our milch camels.""**"
"8419","Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ heard a man say take it green, and replied at your service, we take your omen from your mouth; go out with us to greenery. They went and no sword was drawn. > **""At your service, we take your omen from your mouth; go out with us to greenery.""**"
"8420","Umm Kurz al-Kabiyyah رضي الله عنها reports hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to leave birds upon their roosts. > **""Leave birds upon their roosts.""**"
"8421","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the evil eye, by Allah's permission, obsesses a man until he climbs a height then falls from it. > **""The evil eye, by Allah's permission, obsesses a man until he climbs a height then falls from it.""**"
"8422","Asma bint Umays رضي الله عنها reports hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say half of what is dug for his nation of graves is from the eye. > **""Half of what is dug for my nation of graves is from the eye.""**"
"8423","Jabir ibn Abdullah رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said most who die of his nation after Allah's Book, decree, and predestination die from souls, meaning the eye, as al-Bazzar says. > **""Most who die of my nation after Allah's Book, decree, and predestination die from souls.""**"
"8424","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the evil eye is real, bringing down the height. > **""The evil eye is real, bringing down the height.""**"
"8425","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the evil eye is real, attended by Satan and the envy of Adam's son. In the Sahih only the portion the eye is real is established. > **""The evil eye is real, and Satan and the envy of Adam's son attend it.""**"
"8426","Sahl ibn Hunayf رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ went out with him toward Makkah until at the ravine of Kharrar in Juhfah. Sahl, a fair handsome man of body and skin, bathed, and Amir ibn Rabiah of Banu Adi ibn Kab looked at him saying he never saw like today, not even a veiled maiden's skin. Sahl was smitten. Brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ unable to lift his head or recover, he asked whom they suspect. They named Amir. He summoned Amir, rebuked him asking on what grounds one kills his brother, why he did not bless when admiring, then ordered him to wash. He washed face, hands, elbows, knees, feet edges, and inside his waist-wrapper in a bowl. A man poured it over Sahl's head and back from behind, then cast the bowl behind, and Sahl went with the people unharmed. Al-Tabarani adds he drank from it. > **""Do you suspect anyone concerning him? On what grounds does one of you kill his brother? When you see what pleases you, why did you not bless? Wash.""**"
"8427","In another narration of al-Tabarani an Ansari man passed, with wording asking what prevents one when seeing in his brother what pleases him in self or wealth from blessing him, for the eye is real. > **""What prevents one of you, when he sees in his brother what pleases him in himself or his wealth, from blessing him? For the eye is real.""**"
"8428","Sahl ibn Hunayf رضي الله عنه reports he went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until at Kharrar he entered water to bathe, being a handsome man. Amir ibn Rabiah passed and said he never saw beauty like today, not even a veiled maiden's skin. Sahl was felled at once. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ supplicated for him asking on what grounds one kills his brother and whom they suspect. They named Amir. He summoned Amir, called for a vessel of water, ordered Amir to wash his face, limb edges, knees, feet edges in the water, then the Prophet ﷺ took Amir's waist-wrapper sides and inside, immersed them, poured the vessel over Sahl's head, overturned it behind his back, and Sahl was released unharmed. > **""On what grounds does one of you kill his brother? Whom do you suspect concerning him?""**"
"8429","In a narration the wording is the eye is real. Al-Tabarani transmits with two chains, one of Sahih men save Muhammad ibn Abi Umamah, trustworthy, narrating Abu Umamah's hadith as Ibn Majah narrates, save addition, as reckoned, that he ordered him to sip sips from it. > **""The eye is real.""**"
"8430","Amir ibn Rabiah رضي الله عنه reports he and Sahl ibn Hunayf went seeking asses, found asses and a pool. Each shy to bathe observed, Sahl screened from him, removed his woolen outer cloak, entered water. He looked a glance admiring his build and struck him with his eye. Sahl seized with shivering in the water, unanswering his call. He went to the Prophet ﷺ informing, who said its heat, cold, and ailment departed, ordered him rise, then taught when one sees in self, wealth, or brother what pleases, let him bless, for the eye is real. Ibn Majah narrates only the eye is real. > **""Its heat, cold, and ailment have departed. Rise. When one of you sees in himself, his wealth, or his brother what pleases him, let him bless, for the eye is real.""**"
"8431","Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri describes the washing he found the scholars practice, with the one who cast the eye brought a bowl of water held raised from the ground, washing face once into the bowl with right then left hands, arms to elbows, chest once, back of right palm, right elbow to neck then left likewise, tops of right and left feet from toe roots, backs of right then left knees, immersing the right inner waist-wrapper, then the holder pouring the bowl over the afflicted's head from behind and overturning the bowl behind him upon the ground."
"8432","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever sees something admiring and says what Allah wills, no power but Allah's, it will not harm him. Ibn Abd al-Barr in al-Tamhid cites scholars explaining why did you not bless him as meaning O Allah bless him, and some as blessed is Allah best of creators. More such narrations come in remembrances, Allah willing. > **""Whoever sees something and admires it, and says: What Allah wills, no power but Allah's, it will not harm him.""**"
"8433","Ali, meaning Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه, reports that the Prophet ﷺ ordered skulls erected in crops. Asked why, he said on account of the eye. > **""On account of the eye.""**"
"8434","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said a nation shall enter Paradise altogether, who neither seek ruqyah nor cauterize, trusting their Lord. Sound narrations on entering Paradise without reckoning are established. > **""A nation shall enter Paradise altogether, who neither seek ruqyah, nor cauterize, trusting their Lord.""**"
"8435","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said three are of magic: incantations, tiwalah, and amulets. Ali ibn Yazid explains tiwalah as a woman bewitching her husband to love her. > **""Three are of magic: incantations, tiwalah, and amulets.""**"
"8436","Jabalah ibn al-Azraq رضي الله عنه, among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Dhuhr or Asr with companions beside a very stony wall. Sitting after two rakahs, a scorpion emerged and stung him, he fainted, people performed ruqyah. Awaking he said Allah healed him, not their ruqyah. > **""Allah healed me, not your ruqyah.""**"
"8437","Jabir ibn Abdullah رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ said to Asma bint Umays رضي الله عنها asking why his brother's sons are lean, whether need afflicts them. She said no, but the eye hastens to them, shall they be charmed. He asked with what. She presented it, and he said charm them. > **""What is with my brother's sons lean? Are they afflicted by need? With what? Charm them.""**"
"8438","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that when the Prophet ﷺ complained, Gabriel عليه السلام charmed him saying in Allah's name he charms him from every disease to heal him, from the evil of an envier when envying, and every possessor of an eye. > **""In Allah's name I charm you, from every disease to heal you, from the evil of an envier when he envies, and from the evil of every possessor of an eye.""**"
"8439","Ubadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه reports visiting the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in severe pain known to Allah تبارك وتعالى, then visiting at evening fully healed. Asked, the Prophet ﷺ said O son of al-Samit, Gabriel عليه السلام charmed him with a charm and he healed, shall he teach it. He said yes. He said in Allah's name he charms from all harming, from every envier's envy and eye, and name Allah to heal. > **""O son of al-Samit, Gabriel charmed me with a charm and I healed; shall I teach it to you? In Allah's name I charm you from all that harms you, from every envier's envy and eye; and name Allah to heal you.""**"
"8440","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما raises to the Prophet ﷺ that these words are medicine for every disease, seeking refuge in Allah's perfect words and all His names general, from the evil of venomous and crawling creatures, the afflicting eye, envier when envying, father of Qutrah and his offspring; thirty-three angels come to their Lord complaining ailment from their land, He says take from your earth and wipe your afflicted with Muhammad's ﷺ charm; whoever takes wage or conceals it never prospers. Al-Tabarani in al-Awsat adds by our land and take dust from your earth. > **""These words are medicine for every disease: I seek refuge in Allah's perfect words and all His names general, from the evil of venomous and crawling creatures, the afflicting eye, envier when he envies, father of Qutrah and his offspring. Thirty-three angels came to their Lord saying: ailment from our land; He said: take from your earth and wipe your afflicted; it is Muhammad's charm. Whoever takes wage for it or conceals it never prospers.""**"
"8441","Uthman ibn Affan رضي الله عنه reports falling ill while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited him. One day he charmed him saying in the name of Allah the Merciful Compassionate, he shelters him with Allah the One Eternal Who neither begets nor is born nor has equal, from the evil of what he finds. Standing, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said O Uthman seek refuge thereby, never seeking refuge with its like. > **""In the name of Allah the Merciful Compassionate, I shelter you with Allah the One Eternal Who neither begets nor is born nor has equal, from the evil of what you find. O Uthman, seek refuge thereby, for you never seek refuge with its like.""**"
"8442","Jabir ibn Abdullah رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said no ruqyah but for eye or sting. > **""No ruqyah but for eye or sting.""**"
"8443","Maymunah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ licensed ruqyah against every venomous sting."
"8444","Ubadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه reports he charmed against eye fever in Jahiliyyah. Embracing Islam he mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said present it. He presented, and he said charm thereby, no harm. But for that he would never charm anyone. > **""Present it to me. Charm thereby, no harm in it.""**"
"8445","Ali رضي الله عنه reports a scorpion stung the Prophet ﷺ while praying. Finishing he cursed the scorpion sparing neither worshipper nor other, called for water and salt, wiped over it reciting the Disbelievers, the Daybreak, and Mankind chapters. > **""Allah curse the scorpion, sparing neither worshipper nor other.""**"
"8446","Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports a sting charm mentioned before the Prophet ﷺ, who said present it. They presented: in Allah's name, Qarniyyah, Shajjah, sea salt, Qift. He said these are covenants Solomon عليه السلام took over vermin, seeing no harm. A man with Alqamah stung was charmed thereby and rose as freed from fetters. > **""Present it to me. These are covenants Solomon took over vermin; I see no harm in it.""**"
"8447","Abdullah ibn Zayd رضي الله عنه reports they presented a sting charm to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he permitted it saying they are but covenants. The charm: in Allah's name, Shajjah, Qarniyyah, sea salt. > **""They are but covenants.""**"
"8448","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports an Ansari Amr ibn Hannah who charmed snakebite came saying the Prophet ﷺ forbade charms while he charms snakes. He said recite it. He recited, and he said no harm, these are covenants. Another Ansari charming scorpions came, and he said whoever can benefit his brother let him do so. In the Sahih abridged. > **""Recite it to me. No harm in this; these are covenants. Whoever can benefit his brother let him do so.""**"
"8449","Abdullah رضي الله عنه saw in a household woman's neck a cord with amulets, stretched his hand severely cutting it, and said were one of them to supplicate with water sprinkled on head and face, then say in Allah's name and recite the Sincerity, Daybreak, and Mankind chapters, it would benefit her Allah willing."
"8450","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit and Buraydah رضي الله عنه report the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complained of udhrah until it pained his head and showed upon him. Gabriel came saying his Lord sent him to charm him. The Prophet ﷺ uncovered his head, and he said in Allah's name he charms him from all evil harming, from every envier's eye, repeating thrice, and the Prophet ﷺ healed. > **""In Allah's name I charm you from all evil harming you, from the evil of every envier's eye I charm you.""**"
"8451","Hafsah رضي الله عنها reports the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while a woman called al-Shifa charmed ant bites. The Prophet ﷺ told her to teach it to Hafsah. > **""Teach it to Hafsah.""**"
"8452","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon them finding a complaining boy. Asked, they said only the eye. He asked why they do not charm him against the eye. > **""What is with him? Why do you not charm him against the eye?""**"
"8453","Muhammad ibn Hatib رضي الله عنه reports something from a pot spilled upon his hand. His mother took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a place. He spoke words containing remove harm Lord of men, as reckoned and heal for Thou art Healer, and would spit. > **""Remove harm, Lord of men; and heal, for Thou art the Healer.""**"
"8454","Muhammad ibn Hatib رضي الله عنه reports drawn near a boiling pot, inserting his hand, it burned or swelled. His mother took him to a man at Batha who spoke and blew. In Uthman's rule he asked his mother who the man was. She said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."
"8455","In his narration his mother took him to a man sitting at the graveyard. She said O Messenger of Allah, and he said at your service and happiness. She drew him near, he blew and spoke unknown words. Asked later, his mother said he said remove harm Lord of men, heal Thou art Healer, no healer but Thou. > **""At your service and happiness. Remove harm, Lord of men; heal, Thou art the Healer, no healer but Thou.""**"
"8456","Muhammad ibn Hatib رضي الله عنه reports from Umm Jamil bint al-Mujallal, his mother, that she came with him from Abyssinia until a night or two from Medina. Cooking, firewood finished, she went seeking it, he took the pot overturning it upon his forearm. She brought him to the Prophet ﷺ saying with father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, this is Muhammad ibn Hatib. He spat in his mouth, wiped his head, supplicated, spat upon his hand saying remove suffering Lord of men, heal Thou art Healer, no healing but Thine, healing leaving no sickness. She said she had not risen with him from him before his hand healed. Al-Tabarani adds he is first named after him. > **""Remove suffering, Lord of men; heal, Thou art the Healer, no healing but Thine, healing leaving no sickness.""**"
"8457","Muhammad ibn Hatib رضي الله عنه reports the pot fell upon his hand burning it. His father took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who spat upon it saying remove suffering Lord of men, as reckoned and heal for Thou art Healer. > **""Remove suffering, Lord of men; and heal, for Thou art the Healer.""**"
"8458","Al-Saib ibn Yazid رضي الله عنه reports the Messenger of Allah ﷺ charmed him with the Opening of the Book with spittle."
"8459","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Saib al-Hilali, nephew of Maymunah رضي الله عنها, reports Maymunah said come nephew I charm you with the Messenger's ﷺ charm, saying in Allah's name she charms him, Allah heals him from every disease in him, remove suffering Lord of men, heal no healer but Thou. > **""In Allah's name I charm you, Allah heals you from every disease in you; remove suffering, Lord of men; heal, no healer but Thou.""**"
"8460","Ali رضي الله عنه reports the Prophet ﷺ used to shelter Hasan and Husayn saying he shelters them with Allah's perfect words from every Satan and vermin and every afflicting eye. > **""I shelter you with Allah's perfect words from every Satan and vermin and every afflicting eye.""**"
"8461","Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Husayn and Hasan passed as boys. He said bring his two sons to shelter them as Ibrahim sheltered his sons Ismail and Ishaq, saying he shelters them with Allah's perfect words from every afflicting eye, every Satan and vermin. > **""Bring my two sons to shelter them as Ibrahim sheltered his sons Ismail and Ishaq. I shelter you with Allah's perfect words from every afflicting eye, every Satan and vermin.""**"
"8462","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports the Prophet ﷺ used to shelter Hasan and Husayn saying he shelters them with Allah's perfect words from the evil of what He created, originated, and made. > **""I shelter you with Allah's perfect words from the evil of what He created, originated, and made.""**"
"8463","Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah رضي الله عنه reports the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl until at Harrah a snake bit Abd al-Rahman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said call Amr ibn Hazm. He presented his charm, he said no harm, charm him. Ibn Hazm placed his hand saying O Messenger of Allah he dies or died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said charm him even if dying or dead. He charmed, Abd al-Rahman recovered and departed. > **""Call Amr ibn Hazm to me. No harm in it, charm him. Charm him even if he dies or has died.""**"
"8464","Rafi ibn Khadij رضي الله عنه reports the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Ibn Nuayman saying remove suffering Lord of men, God of men. > **""Remove suffering, Lord of men, God of men.""**"
"8465","Ammar ibn Yasir رضي الله عنه reports entering upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while feverish. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked shall he teach a charm Gabriel عليه السلام charmed him with. He said yes O Messenger of Allah. He said in Allah's name he charms him, Allah heals him from every concerning disease; take it congratulations. More narrations on morning evening sayings and seeking refuge come in remembrances, Allah willing. > **""Shall I teach you a charm Gabriel charmed me with? In Allah's name I charm you, Allah heals you from every disease concerning you; take it, congratulations.""**"
"8466","Kab ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when one finds pain let him place his hand beneath his pain then say seven times he seeks refuge in Allah's might and power over all things from the evil of what he finds. > **""When one of you finds pain, let him place his hand beneath his pain then say seven times: I seek refuge in Allah's might and power over all things from the evil of what I find.""**"
"8467","Ubayy ibn Kab رضي الله عنه reports with the Prophet ﷺ when a Bedouin came saying O Prophet of Allah his brother suffers pain. Asked its nature, he said touch of madness. He said bring him. Placed before him, the Prophet ﷺ charmed him with the Opening, first four verses of the Cow, the two verses and Allah's god is One God, the Throne verse, last three of the Cow, a verse of Imran's Family Allah bears witness, a verse of the Heights surely your Lord is Allah, the last of the Believers exalted is Allah the True King, a verse of the Jinn exalted is our Lord's grandeur, first ten of the Ranks, first three of the Gathering, the Sincerity, and the two Seekers of Refuge. The man rose as never complaining."
"8468","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla reports from a man, from his father, that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ saying his brother aches. Asked, he said touch of madness. He said send him to me. He sat before him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the Opening, first four of the Cow, a middle verse and Allah's god is One God to the end of the creation of heavens and earth verse, then likewise with ten verses of the Ranks not from its beginning, and three last of the Gathering."
"8469","Hanash al-Sanani reports from Abdullah that he recited in an afflicted's ear and he awoke. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked what he recited. He said did you think We created you in vain, to the chapter's end. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said had a certain man recited it upon a mountain it would shift. Narrations on wellness from jinn without charm by his ﷺ blessing come in prophetic signs. > **""What did you recite in his ear? Had a certain man recited it upon a mountain it would shift.""**"
"8470","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports a woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking supplication for healing. He said if she wishes he supplicates Allah to heal her, and if she wishes she endures with no reckoning upon her. She chose endurance with no reckoning. > **""If you wish I supplicate Allah to heal you, and if you wish endure with no reckoning upon you.""**"
"8471","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Prophet ﷺ said whoever sleeps after Asr then his mind is snatched, let him blame none but himself. > **""Whoever sleeps after Asr then his mind is snatched, let him blame none but himself.""**"
"8472","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said man is exposed at four traits: sleeping alone, sleeping on his back, sleeping in a saffron-dyed sheet, and bathing in open land. Whoever can avoid bathing in open land, and if must, let him draw a line. > **""Man is exposed at four traits: when he sleeps alone, sleeps on his back, sleeps in a saffron-dyed sheet, and bathes in open land. Whoever can avoid bathing in open land, and if he must, let him draw a line.""**"
"8473","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said a prophet among prophets used to draw lines, so whoever agrees with his knowledge, it is his knowledge. > **""A prophet among prophets used to draw lines; whoever agrees with his knowledge, it is his knowledge.""**"
"8474","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said O Ali perfect ablution though hard, eat not charity, breed not asses upon horses, and sit not with astrologers. Abu Dawud and al-Nasai narrate the asses upon horses portion. > **""O Ali, perfect ablution though hard upon you, eat not charity, breed not asses upon horses, and sit not with astrologers.""**"
"8475","Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib رضي الله عنه reports going out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Medina. He turned to it saying Allah has cleared this peninsula of polytheism. > **""Verily Allah has cleared this peninsula of polytheism.""**"
"8476","In a narration Allah has purified this town of polytheism if stars do not misguide them. Abu Yala and al-Tabarani transmit in the Large and Middle, with Qays ibn al-Rabi deemed trustworthy by Shubah and al-Thawri, weakened by others. > **""Verily Allah has purified this town of polytheism, if stars do not misguide them.""**"
"8477","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade looking into stars."
"8478","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said many a teacher of Abjad letters studying stars has no share with Allah on Resurrection Day. > **""Many a teacher of Abjad letters studying stars has no share with Allah on Resurrection Day.""**"
"8479","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not of us is who takes omens or has them taken, practices soothsaying or has it practiced, practices magic or has it practiced. > **""Not of us is who takes omens or has omens taken for him, practices soothsaying or has it practiced for him, practices magic or has it practiced for him.""**"
"8480","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not of us is who takes omens or has them taken, practices soothsaying or has it practiced, practices magic or has it practiced, ties a knot or has it tied, and whoever visits a diviner believing what he says disbelieves in what descended upon Muhammad ﷺ. Narrations on the sorcerer's killing come at the end of prescribed punishments, Allah willing. > **""Not of us is who takes omens or has omens taken for him, practices soothsaying or has it practiced for him, practices magic or has it practiced for him, ties a knot or has a knot tied for him; and whoever visits a diviner believing what he says disbelieves in what descended upon Muhammad.""**"
"8481","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said take the white rooster, for a house with a white rooster is approached by neither Satan nor sorcerer, nor the houses around it. > **""Take the white rooster, for a house with a white rooster is approached by neither Satan nor sorcerer, nor the houses around it.""**"
"8482","Jabir ibn Abdullah رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ that whoever visits a diviner believing what he says disbelieves in what descended upon Muhammad ﷺ. > **""Whoever visits a diviner believing what he says disbelieves in what descended upon Muhammad.""**"
"8483","Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه reports hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say whoever visits a seer, his prayer is not accepted forty nights. > **""Whoever visits a seer, his prayer is not accepted forty nights.""**"
"8484","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever visits a seer, his prayer is not accepted forty nights. > **""Whoever visits a seer, his prayer is not accepted forty nights.""**"
"8485","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever visits a diviner believing what he says is absolved from what descended upon Muhammad ﷺ, and whoever visits unbelieving, his prayer is not accepted forty nights. > **""Whoever visits a diviner believing what he says is absolved from what descended upon Muhammad; and whoever visits him unbelieving, his prayer is not accepted forty nights.""**"
"8486","Wathilah ibn al-Asqa رضي الله عنه reports hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say whoever visits a diviner asking about something, repentance is veiled from him forty nights; if he believes what he says he disbelieves. In his narration if he has faith in what he says instead of believes him. > **""Whoever visits a diviner asking about something, repentance is veiled from him forty nights; if he believes what he says he disbelieves.""**"
"8487","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the high ranks shall never attain who practices divination, seeks lots, or returns from travel by omen. > **""The high ranks shall never attain who practices divination, seeks lots, or returns from travel by omen.""**"
"8488","In a narration if he takes an omen turning him from travel, he shall not look upon the high ranks. > **""If he takes an omen turning him from travel, he shall not look upon the high ranks.""**"
"8489","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, says whoever visits a seer or diviner believing what he says disbelieves in what descended upon Muhammad ﷺ."
"8490","Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه says whoever visits a seer, sorcerer, or diviner, asks him and believes what he says, disbelieves in what descended upon Muhammad ﷺ."
